  "findings": [
    "March19/2026 minutes page4 record unanimous voice-vote approval of Resolution2026-03-003. Attached PDFpage53 is signed/sealed, effective on passage, and bars accepting zoning petitions for energy-storage systems/power stations untilMay21/2026. Its operative clause does not make expiry contingent on state implementing regulations.",
    "May21/2026 minutes page4 record unanimous voice-vote approval of Resolution2026-05-004. Attached signed/sealed PDFpage11 is effective on passage and setsJune23/2026 as the endpoint. The anticipated ordinance vote in its recital also saysJune23; this is preserved, not silently changed toJune25.",
    "June25 minutes page4 record approval of Ordinance2026-06-004. The ordinance supplies storage regulations; it is not treated as the event ending a resolution whose printed endpoint wasJune23. The actual two-day transition and any other intervening act remain unverified.",
    "September24 andOctober22 minute-bundle OCR screening did not locate moratorium/energy-storage/TOD text; this is not exhaustive proof of absence of later action. July/August full minutes were not reviewed in this phase.",
    "Current county TOD routing page repeats November19/2026 at11:59pm subject to board modification and says no petitions pending. This is an attributed observation, not a complete independent current-force or project-file audit."
  ],
